<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sierra Morena</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sierra Morena is a mountain range in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> separating the central plateau from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalquivir">Guadalquivir</a> valley. Rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>, lead and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, its mines were worked by Iberian peoples and later by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castulo">Castulo</a> grew wealthy from them. Its silver helped pay for the Barcid armies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sierra-morena.jpg" alt="Sierra Morena" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NacionAndaluza · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valles_t%C3%ADpicos_de_Obejo,_Sierra_Morena.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
